<title>UK: Details of Nov dip in Britain car registrations.</title>
<headline>Details of Nov dip in Britain car registrations.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's SMMT Ltd auto trade body issued the folowing details of new car registrations for November showing how registrations dipped by 5.4 percent in the month, to give a 3.9 percent rise for the year so far.</p>
<p>November</p>
<p>Top 10 by marque, market share in pct vs year ago.</p>
<p> Ford	   21,960  (16.23 pct) vs  30,779  (21.52 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall  19,172  (14.17 pct) vs  22,170  (15.50 pct)</p>
<p> Rover	  18,409  (13.60 pct) vs  23,855  (16.68 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	11,033   (8.15 pct) vs   9,051   (6.33 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	 8,133   (6.01 pct) vs   7,275   (5.09 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen 7,609   (5.62 pct) vs   6,422   (4.49 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan     5,953   (4.40 pct) vs   5,918   (4.14 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat	 5,925   (4.38 pct) vs   4,524   (3.16 pct)</p>
<p> BMW	  4,359   (3.22 pct) vs   3,259   (2.28 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen   4,314   (3.19 pct) vs   5,546   (3.88 pct)</p>
<p>Top 10 marques year to date, market share in pct vs yr ago.</p>
<p> Ford		  382,099 (19.62 pct) vs 399,810  (21.34 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall	 273,879 (14.06 pct) vs 283,181  (15.11 pct)</p>
<p> Rover		 208,453 (10.70 pct) vs 223,151  (11.91 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	     147,888  (7.59 pct) vs 139,037   (7.42 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	     129,371  (6.64 pct) vs 118,463   (6.32 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen	  109,815  (5.64 pct) vs  78,618   (4.20 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan		 90,034  (4.62 pct) vs  87,682   (4.68 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat		   81,989  (4.21 pct) vs  67,412   (3.60 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen		74,187  (3.81 pct) vs  78,013   (4.16 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota    58,938  (3.03 pct) vs  52,832   (2.82 pct)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
